From e01ae19e4438addf1350cbb5614c9910ef61c7d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:35:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: anatop USB_ANALOG overlay + PHY VBUS bits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two fixes for USB charger detection:
- imx-usb-phy: report VBUS_VLD and BVALID in PHY STATUS register
- fsl-imx6sx: overlay the anatop USB_ANALOG registers (VBUS_DETECT_STAT
  at +0x1C0 and CHRG_DETECT_STAT at +0x240) so the imx_usb_charger
  driver sees VBUS present

Gets past 'vbus is error' (EINVAL) to 'VBUS is coming from a dedicated
power supply', but charger TYPE detection still fails with ENXIO (-6) —
the DCD/primary-detect sequence needs a proper state machine in the
overlay. The gadget binds regardless; the gap is nlclient's USB observer
which keys off the power_supply 'present' attribute.
